WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.850
- All hour, we've celebrated rad dads.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.577
And while I saved a very
special dad for the end

00:00:05.577 --> 00:00:06.639
this is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.690
(bouncy music)

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.880
So fathers are known
for giving life advice

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.920
whether it's cars, money, relationships

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.720
or maybe even how to caulk a sink.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.130
Um, and thanks to TikTok.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.200
A dad from Washington
State is giving that kind

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.670
of advice to millions.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.900
Just take a look.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.850
- I'm gonna show you how
to check your oil today.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.560
It's really easy to do.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.560
Just make sure your
automobile is relatively level

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.840
and that it's been sitting for a while.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.970
Then the big fish is gonna swim on

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.173
the backside of the
rock. Come over the top.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.540
I know it's hard to see

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.440
and the big fish is gonna drop
down through the waterfall.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.703
Then you cinch it up.

00:00:45.568 --> 00:00:48.048
- Oh my God. I love the big fish.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.940
Bo started the Tiktok channel
called Dad Advice from Bo

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.877
with daughter, Emily. I love it.

00:00:52.877 --> 00:00:54.930
And we have him on the line now.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.208
What's up Bo? What's up Emily?

00:00:58.208 --> 00:01:00.570
- Hey, nice to see you.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.610
- [Kelly] OK. So I, Bo, I'm assuming

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.580
that this was more Emily's idea at first.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.110
- Oh, absolutely.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.400
In real life I'm actually
a very private person.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.660
So when Emily proposed this idea to me

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.280
I immediately rejected it.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.430
I didn't wanna have anything to do with it

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.780
but she's very persistent.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.610
She kept coming back to me day

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.310
after day and she always
had a new reason to do it.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.140
A new idea for me.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.070
And then she came up

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.580
with this one this one
day where she said, listen

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.980
you have a dad that
you're always able to go

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.260
to for advice whenever you
want, which I still do.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.109
And all the kids have you.

00:01:41.109 --> 00:01:41.970
But what

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.174
if there's somebody out there
that doesn't have a dad?

00:01:44.174 --> 00:01:45.007
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:01:45.007 --> 00:01:45.840
- What if there's somebody out there

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.130
that could use that kind of advice?

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:50.130
Don't you wanna make some videos for them?

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.750
Yeah, I, I had to agree.
That's not a bad idea. So,

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.583
- [Kelly] Yeah

00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.400
- We started making a couple of videos

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.480
and the responses that we've
gotten have been just amazing.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.940
- Yeah. And she's, she's totally right.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:03.780
Emily's totally right.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.510
Some of us didn't grow
up with a dad around.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.160
Luckily I did have some good guy friends

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.420
that did tell me how to, you know

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.250
change the tire and do
my oil, change my oil.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.630
But, but there's Emily.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.370
There's another reason that
you started this channel.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.840
Can you share that with us?

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.240
- Yeah. I wish that it
was just a genius idea

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.430
but it was really born out of desperation.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.680
I suffered a traumatic brain injury

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.440
in a soccer game and it
happened to the back of my head.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.410
So you can't see it on my
face, but my body is very sick.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.830
And so in 2020, try not to cry.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.060
I just said to my parents, like

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.770
I don't wanna keep fighting anymore.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.060
I don't have anything left in me.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:39.090
And so starting the TikTok
was just my attempt to

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.040
do something every day.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.100
And I thought I could put
something good out in the world

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.450
but what we got was an army

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.200
of people just fighting for me
and telling me to keep going.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.940
And I don't, there's a
lot of people with my type

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.770
of brain injury in the world
and a lot of good dads.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.650
So I don't know why we got
chosen to have this blessing

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.620
but we will do everything
we can to pay it forward.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.840
- Absolutely. How are you
doing right now? Emily?

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.610
Are you doing better?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.480
- I'm okay.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.010
I'm fighting really hard.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:08.700
And because of TikTok and
the money we've earned

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.400
I get to go to a brain
injury clinic next week

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.280
and try to get really, really well.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.201
- Okay, alright. Hey, well
please, please let us know

00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:20.121
if we can help in any way.

00:03:20.121 --> 00:03:22.041
I didn't know that part of this story.

00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:23.250
So please let us know if we can help.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.290
And I have to say, is
this where y'all live?

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.673
This beautiful log cabin?

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.730
- Yeah, we are very lucky.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.470
- In the, in the middle of the woods.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.303
- Oh my God.

00:03:32.303 --> 00:03:34.470
- We just wanted to say
your whole show is just

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.810
about good people and how much
good there is in the world.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.030
And I think in the last couple of years

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.410
a lot of people started to question that

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.490
but we just wanna reiterate.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.430
There is so much good in this world.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.293
- Absolutely. Emily. You are. Emily. Woo.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.660
You're breaking me right now.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.780
Oh my God. I wish you were
here. I wanna hug you.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.920
I don't know where you are, but I'd come.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.753
I love a log cabin

00:03:56.753 --> 00:03:58.500
and I love being out in
the middle of nowhere

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.000
says the girl who owns a ranch in Montana.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.130
So I'm, I'm down with wherever you are.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.660
Thank y'all so much and good luck

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.460
with whatever treatment
you're gonna, you're gonna do.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.100
And, and let us know, please,
if we can help you in any way.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.900
Bo thank you so much for
helping everybody out there

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.660
that maybe didn't have a daddy
to teach him stuff like that.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.623
I'm liking y'all's post right now

00:04:14.623 --> 00:04:16.830
(chime)

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:20.400
and I'm still wiping away
tears, but that's not all.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.280
Our season long partner,
pilot pen makers of G2.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.990
The go to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.030
Want to honor ultimate overachievers.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:27.863
Just like y'all.

00:04:27.863 --> 00:04:28.860
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:29.700
for a thousand dollars.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.550
How's that sound?

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.879
All right?

00:04:34.879 --> 00:04:35.712
- [Emily] Oh my gosh.

00:04:35.712 --> 00:04:36.545
- All right!

00:04:36.545 --> 00:04:37.378
I love you guys.

00:04:37.378 --> 00:04:38.940
God bless, good luck.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.133
And thank you so much for joining us.

